{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/395882-fixing-the-desacrated-locus","id":395882,"title":"Fixing the desacrated Locus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-06T23:50:35-08:00","id":395882,"title":"Fixing the desacrated Locus","content":"So on our last session my Swedish pack found out that after being beaten and drove of their Locus by the Bale Hounds pack, the Maelejin servants have &quot;desecrated&quot; this place. Their Totem also do not answer their calls. Question is simple: <b>What could happen to the Locus or the Totem, rules-wise?</b><br /> <br /> Locus is on the ancient sacred ground of Sami people where animals comes to die, especially the bears. Because of this, it's called by spirits and shapechangers the &quot;Bear Cemetary&quot;. In Flesh it's only couple of rocks covered in snow, with sacred stone in center. In Shadow it looks like this...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://images.wikia.com/lionking/images/b/b2/ElephantGraveyard2.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> The Totem of the pack is Bear Spirit of Star for the Dead called &quot;Light of the Dead&quot;. He is shown as radiating bear form as the star on the night sky that is ever present under the Locus. And his light is guiding the dead to their resting place, in the dark of sky.<br /> <br /> So what kind bad things could happen to Locus and Totem by the paws of Bale Hounds? I think the simplest for Totem is that he was killed by them and now need to reform in Shadow. But what other things could happen? Bale Hounds were at least a full day in this location, to do their evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T05:12:24-08:00","id":396154,"title":"","content":"The obvious thing would be to drink all the Essence out of the Locus then trash it so badly (breaking the sacred stone and tumbling it over, etc) as to functionally destroy the Locus until such a time as it can reform, which could be weeks given the disruption. Have them leave behind some traumatised, crippled humans all tied up or whatnot.<br /> <br /> Not only are the wounded humans a problem for the pack - some local humans just went missing and following the blood trail will lead to some sort of bloody scene at the pack's Locus, which law enforcement will probably think means there's a lunatic cult on the loose and will start investigating the kinds of things the pack really don't want them to - but it's a clear sign and lure dangled before them by the Bale Hounds. Your nice, safe source of Essence is gone, they're saying. Time to start being real predators. We've left you these two snacks to get started on. You want Essence, you're gonna have to get used to consuming the flesh of the herd. A good way for the Bale Hounds to try and force the pack off the path of the Oath of the Moon and into a cycle of degeneration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T08:13:14-08:00","id":396380,"title":"","content":"I like that a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T08:36:30-08:00","id":396391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/395882-fixing-the-desacrated-locus?p=396154#post396154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The obvious thing would be to drink all the Essence out of the Locus then trash it so badly (breaking the sacred stone and tumbling it over, etc) as to functionally destroy the Locus until such a time as it can reform, which could be weeks given the disruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>Were are rules for rebuilding destroyed Locus in this way? In Appendix of 1ed corebook? Are there other solutions in 2ed setting? ( We are using elements of 2ed from spoilers so maybe use this? )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/395882-fixing-the-desacrated-locus?p=396154#post396154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have them leave behind some traumatized, crippled humans all tied up or whatnot.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be very good, as the Bale Hounds made almost all the nearby town possessed by Maeljin servants. They can make a bloody sacrifices on them to make a more lasting <b>Inferno</b>'s desecration here. Maybe I even look in to <b>Inferno</b>'s rules for Malus Loci?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/395882-fixing-the-desacrated-locus?p=396154#post396154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not only are the wounded humans a problem for the pack - some local humans just went missing and following the blood trail will lead to some sort of bloody scene at the pack's Locus, which law enforcement will probably think means there's a lunatic cult on the loose and will start investigating the kinds of things the pack really don't want them to - but it's a clear sign and lure dangled before them by the Bale Hounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice idea for normal Werewolf game, but not usable in this particular case. As Bale Hounds pack is running local small town ( about 900 people ) and made people Possesed by Maeljin demons. On the other hand, I marked they used the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/319914-legion-corrupted-spirits\">Legion of 49 them</a>, so players would only assume there are abuot 5% of population in real possesion. Rest is probably too afraid and locked in the valley covered by snow from at least the month. And demons do not needed to be too much explicit about their influence - in the Bale Hounds pack there is major, local pastor, library lady, prominent reindeer breeder lady and monstrous <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ephemera-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">Urhanu</a> ( wolf-based Uratha ) that is local towns legend. Not too mentioned sexual predator psychopath. With the lead of previous Alpha ( apex huntsman, killed by PCs ) and consul of Beta ( the pastor ), they just slowly over taken this small community. Now they are ruling it from shadows. Even one of three police officers is consumed by Wrath spirit. So I do not see the Police as a real problem for the PCs Pack. But they could be turn in by them to help fight the Bale Hounds secret oppression.<br /> <br /> More, maybe players will need a way to sway a town with them and help fight the Hounds. But how would they?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/395882-fixing-the-desacrated-locus?p=396154#post396154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your nice, safe source of Essence is gone, they're saying. Time to start being real predators. We've left you these two snacks to get started on. You want Essence, you're gonna have to get used to consuming the flesh of the herd. A good way for the Bale Hounds to try and force the pack off the path of the Oath of the Moon and into a cycle of degeneration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made a mistake before and let the players to hunt the meat and spirits for Essence. They just made go hunt the reindeer each night to re pool their Essence. How to stop this? Are not in 2ed rules that past certain Primal Urge the normal meat do not give you sustain? Maybe limit with this? Or made a big spirit rebellion on PCs because of their hunting?<br /> <br /> Connected question to the main of the topic: <b>How can Wound be healed and close the Wound's Realm?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-07-2015, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T08:58:11-08:00","id":396405,"title":"","content":"Answering by own question by the usage of <b>Inferno</b> book, but needing some clarifications. Assuming Bale Hounds made a ritualistic torture and killings in the PCs Loci - it would give the Desecration Rating 3 or 4, that last it's effect on 10 or 25 years. I bet players would not want to wait this long, so let's see the options. From the book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Destroying a Desecrated Place</b><br /> Given enough time, almost any Desecrated place or thing will lose the characteristic taint of evil, but in some cases that\u2019s not fast enough. In these situations, the following options are available. At the Storyteller\u2019s option, they do not function against Desecration ratings of 6 or higher without additional, special criteria.<br /> <br /> \u2022 A Malus Loci can use its Infernal Influence to reduce Desecration levels of its domain, but it will usually do this only within the terms of a pact. These pacts usually include a promise to summon the demon or bar it from returning to Hell. Obviously, this is not any cautious person\u2019s first choice.<br /> <br /> \u2022 It\u2019s possible to destroy a Desecrated object, or alter a Desecrated place to such a degree as to render it unrecognizable. Infernal inhabitants will no doubt interfere with these efforts and, even then, a demon\u2019s Aura of Corruption may leave lasting effects.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Supernatural powers that alter mystical Resonance may be used to reduce the Desecration Ranks. This usually requires 2 successes (or levels of magical Potency) per Rank.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Sincere, moral people can perform an exorcism or a similar cultural rite to cleanse the place. The standard threshold for success is 3 + (double the Desecration rating) If the effort succeeds, the target loses 1 Rank of Desecration.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The simplest method ordinary people can use is to construct a memorial or teaching facility at the location,or present the object in a similar context. The facility should be designed to come to terms with the terrible things connected to the place or object. If a Desecrated knife is presented as evidence at a truly just criminal trial, or the cursed site of a lynching becomes an anti-racist teaching facility that accrued virtue might be enough to reduce or eliminate any lingering Infernal taint. The exact guidelines are left to the Storyteller and her group. </div> </div> </div>The first option is a bit dangerous - to summon a demon so that he will take desacration with himself. As one of PCs is secretly possessed by Pride demon, it could take interesting twist. Logical would be for the PC to try to talk over rest of Pack in to summoning being that is Urging him? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Second one is a bit obvious, but I do not think it will work. If PCs will &quot;clean&quot; the Bear Cemetery, it still be looking like the place it was before. It's a bit point of it - to return to it's normal role as resting place of animals ( and humans ).<br /> <br /> Third option sounds more as mages way to resolve matters.<br /> <br /> Fourth option is interesting in the <b>Werewolf</b> game. I assume The Rite of Chosen Ground would solve this problem, but it's 4th dot Rite, and our Ithaeur just bought 3rd one for the Rite of Healing. Is there any lower Rite that could solve as &quot;spiritual exorcisms&quot;. If not, what kind of spirits could teach The Rite of Chosen Ground to the Pack? And how Pride spirit controlled PC could make it bad? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Fifth option is outside of scope for this chronicle. I suspect it could be used on the Wound in the town itself, after the events of the game, but not for the Loci of PCs that want to retake it as soon as possible.<br /> <br /> Also, next question: <b>Is slain Totem also reform after the time in the Shadow Realm? Would this spirit still be bound by the pact with a Pack? </b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-07-2015, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T09:27:56-08:00","id":396417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/395882-fixing-the-desacrated-locus?p=396391#post396391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Were are rules for rebuilding destroyed Locus in this way? In Appendix of 1ed corebook? Are there other solutions in 2ed setting? ( We are using elements of 2ed from spoilers so maybe use this? )</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some 1e stuff, I think; depends on whether the Locus is just trashed or if they've done Evil Bale Hound Rites (TM) to make it proper gribblified with Wound-taint or whatnot.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It could be very good, as the Bale Hounds made almost all the nearby town possessed by Maeljin servants. They can make a bloody sacrifices on them to make a more lasting <b>Inferno</b>'s desecration here. Maybe I even look in to <b>Inferno</b>'s rules for Malus Loci? </div> </div> </div>No idea, I'm afraid; I've never read Inferno.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I made a mistake before and let the players to hunt the meat and spirits for Essence. They just made go hunt the reindeer each night to re pool their Essence. How to stop this? Are not in 2ed rules that past certain Primal Urge the normal meat do not give you sustain? Maybe limit with this? Or made a big spirit rebellion on PCs because of their hunting? </div> </div> </div>Well with the correct Rites they certainly <i>can</i> hunt spirits for Essence, but:<br /> - They need access to the spirit world to do so. If the Locus is trashed, how exactly are they going to get into the <i>Hisil</i>?<br /> - Rampant spirit predation is likely to result in retaliation from the spirits, more active hostility and spirits banding together to get their revenge on the Uratha.<br /> - Alternatively, rampant spirit predation can result in lots of feeble spirits that are very weak after they've just managed to recorporate, and a powerful or desperate spirit might see them as easy meals. Cue the creation of a magath or other nasty spirit of considerable power that has grown fat from being a vulture to the pack's 'kills' in this way, with plenty of plot ensuing.<br /> - If you've let the player characters get Essence back from <i>normal</i> animal meat then you've majorly changed the balance of how Essence works, the drama and tension around the Oath and the consumption of human flesh, etc. In that case, you're better off talking OC with your players and saying 'I did X but I want Essence and how you get it to be relevant rather than something that's so easy to get, so I would like to change back to the core rules mechanics around acquiring Essence'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Connected question to the main of the topic: <b>How can Wound be healed and close the Wound's Realm?</b> </div> </div> </div>If they actually turn the Locus into a Wound (quite an accomplishment) then the pack are gonna have a hella tough time sorting it - otoh it might still be a 'weak' Wound in the earliest stages of infection, so I'd suggest a medically-minded approach. Go in and clean out the infected tissue, killing any Wounded spirits and burning/cauterising the spiritscape itself with cleansing symbolism, rites and whatever else is possible. Possibly literally incinerate it, although you'd have to be careful that the fire-Essence didn't end up getting Wounded too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T10:59:27-08:00","id":396517,"title":"","content":"Regarding law enforcement, I'm not sure exactly how it works in your area, but here we have a few levels of it. Municipal, which could be small town or big city, big city further being divided up), county, state and federal. If the Bale Hounds do control the town, including the law enforcement, they could possibly send word to neighboring law enforcement agencies that the PCs are murderers and should be apprehended on sight. Especially since they currently control access to the crime scene and can make it look as brutal as possible.<br /> <br /> Since it looks like Maeljin are being tied to Inferno, having them turn the locus into a malus loci seems like it could work. The spirits there would become absorbed or slowly corrupted, with assistance from the Bale Hounds who feed the demon the essence and sin it needs until it can handle it on its own.<br /> <br /> Healing a Wound is supposed to be a ridiculously tough thing to do, as Acro pointed out. Just getting rid of the Lord of the Wound is going to make other spirits take up the title.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T11:03:06-08:00","id":396520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/395882-fixing-the-desacrated-locus?p=396417#post396417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's some 1e stuff, I think; depends on whether the Locus is just trashed or if they've done Evil Bale Hound Rites (TM) to make it proper gribblified with Wound-taint or whatnot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was more thinking about spiritual trashing of Locus by one day, cause there was too little time for proper Wound. But then, <b>Inferno</b> desecration is more like Wound taint, so I think Bale Hounds would be using Evil Bale Hound Rites (TM), just for lower points of it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/395882-fixing-the-desacrated-locus?p=396417#post396417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well with the correct Rites they certainly <i>can</i> hunt spirits for Essence, but:<br /> - They need access to the spirit world to do so. If the Locus is trashed, how exactly are they going to get into the <i>Hisil</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>They have other Keyed Verge in their territory, under the Frozen Waterfall. It is only Verge, so no Essence generation. But they can use it to transit from Flesh to Spirit and in reversal. But it's about 2 hours longer to travel to town than from Bear Cemetery, so they are trying much more to regain their proper Locus - both Essence <b>and</b> travel between realms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/395882-fixing-the-desacrated-locus?p=396417#post396417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Rampant spirit predation is likely to result in retaliation from the spirits, more active hostility and spirits banding together to get their revenge on the Uratha.<br /> - Alternatively, rampant spirit predation can result in lots of feeble spirits that are very weak after they've just managed to recorporate, and a powerful or desperate spirit might see them as easy meals. Cue the creation of a magath or other nasty spirit of considerable power that has grown fat from being a vulture to the pack's 'kills' in this way, with plenty of plot ensuing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both idea are cool - and it's time for reminding players why Uratha <i>do not</i> hunt on spirits on everyday for Essence. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/395882-fixing-the-desacrated-locus?p=396417#post396417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- If you've let the player characters get Essence back from <i>normal</i> animal meat then you've majorly changed the balance of how Essence works, the drama and tension around the Oath and the consumption of human flesh, etc. In that case, you're better off talking OC with your players and saying 'I did X but I want Essence and how you get it to be relevant rather than something that's so easy to get, so I would like to change back to the core rules mechanics around acquiring Essence'.</div> </div> </div> </div>They risen in Primal Urge to level 3-4. Is not in 2ed limit on things that get's them &quot;sustain&quot; on meat of animals - like it was with vampires? I mean, it's what was written in <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/i-got-your-questions-right-here-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">this spoiler</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Keep your Primal Urge low, and you can eat what you like. At higher levels, you can still eat what you like, but you don\u2019t get any nourishment from it. It\u2019s only at Primal Urge 6 that you have to hold to a strict carnivorous diet. Each day that you don\u2019t costs you Essence. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Any nourishment&quot; would mean no Essence, if normal rules would sustaining it. I would just rise a bar to the predatory animals, and PCs will need to hunt wolves or humans - enough &quot;monstrisitation&quot; for PCs. The talk maybe needed, but the rules would also be good to help in the discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/395882-fixing-the-desacrated-locus?p=396417#post396417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they actually turn the Locus into a Wound (quite an accomplishment) then the pack are gonna have a hella tough time sorting it - otoh it might still be a 'weak' Wound in the earliest stages of infection, so I'd suggest a medically-minded approach. Go in and clean out the infected tissue, killing any Wounded spirits and burning/cauterising the spiritscape itself with cleansing symbolism, rites and whatever else is possible. Possibly literally incinerate it, although you'd have to be careful that the fire-Essence didn't end up getting Wounded too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Proper Wound is in the church, in the center of town, that Bale Hounds remaded <i>by years</i> - to now open gates to Hell... Wound Realm, with <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/360414-souless-wolf-as-urfarah-remains\">&quot;Mother Wolf&quot; </a>in it. It is very powerfull Wound that can twist nearby regions. Any help on closeing something like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-07-2015, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T11:18:16-08:00","id":396543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/395882-fixing-the-desacrated-locus?p=396517#post396517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding law enforcement, I'm not sure exactly how it works in your area, but here we have a few levels of it. Municipal, which could be small town or big city, big city further being divided up), county, state and federal. If the Bale Hounds do control the town, including the law enforcement, they could possibly send word to neighboring law enforcement agencies that the PCs are murderers and should be apprehended on sight. Especially since they currently control access to the crime scene and can make it look as brutal as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting is on purpose closed from the external world - the chronicle take place on edge of Sweden, near Scands Mountains, where is starting the Lapland. As weird snow storm is returning for few weeks, closing citizens, PCs and Bale Hounds in few kilometers valley, with the town.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}